cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Calibench, its questions or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Calibench: does a model know what it knows?"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for the calibration of language models' numeric uncertainty. Models answer
  questions with a computable numeric answer, first by instinct and then after working them
  out, each with an estimate and 50% and 90% intervals. Answers are settled only after every
  reply is recorded, and scored with a proper, log-scale weighted interval score, with
  intervals over questions, coverage, and test-retest reliability.
authors:
  - name: "The Neo3 authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmedmah987/Neo3"
url: "https://github.com/ahmedmah987/Neo3/tree/main/calibench"
license:
